    </ul>
    <h2>What I could not verify</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Meta’s current request and response fields when an MMP asks it to claim an install. AppsFlyer documents the direction. I did not find the schema.</li>
      <li>Meta’s field name for an app-install click identifier. “Click id” in this note is a teaching label.</li>
      <li>Whether the AdAttributionKit postback bytes leave the device or an Apple server. The overview says a signed signal from Apple. The framework docs describe delivery to the network’s registered URL. I am not choosing a transport beyond that.</li>
      <li>The numeric crowd-anonymity thresholds for each postback field.</li>
      <li>Which host an Android Attribution API client must use. The page’s main text and its Android sample disagree.</li>
      <li>The exact AppsFlyer screen where the Amplitude API key is entered. Amplitude points to AppsFlyer for that setup, and the English page did not come back in search.</li>
      <li>Any MMP other than AppsFlyer. I did not read their Amplitude integrations, so I did not generalize.</li>
      <li>Whether a given MMP is registered to receive Apple postbacks itself, or only sees what the ad network or the developer forwards.</li>
      <li>How an iOS-only app is treated when AppsFlyer says a non-AMM Meta postback is limited to install-referrer installs. iOS has no Play install referrer, and the paragraph does not spell out that case.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
